<blockquote>
<p><em>Love is memory. In the immediate present we don't love; life is too much with us. We lust, wilt, snort, swallow, gobble, hustle, nuzzle, etc. Later, memory flashes images swathed in nostalgia and yearning. We call that Love. Ha! Better to call it Madness.</em> - John Cage</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p><em><a href="https://youtu.be/2aYT1Pwp30M">I love sounds. Just as they are.</a></em> - John Cage</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Obviously, this is an article about John Cage intercepted by a cult. Were you intending on telling a story about Cage developing a different perspective on sound, by looking at the stars?</p>

